-- title:
--   Transfer of a mod p Hecke eigensystem from level N' to N'p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $W$ a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$, let $N'$ be a nonzero natural number, and let $S_0 \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ be a set containing $p$ and every prime divisor of $N'$. For a level $N$ and a set $S$, `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` denotes the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$; under the hypotheses on $S_0$ the second family is empty both for $N'$ and for $N'p$. Assume given a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_k$ of `heckeAlgebra N' 2 S₀` whose image contains $p$, and such that for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta(W)$ the element $T_\ell - a_\ell(W)$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_k$; here $a_\ell(W) = \ell + 1 - \#(W \bmod \ell)$ is the trace of Frobenius of the reduction of $W$ modulo $\ell$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_2$ of `heckeAlgebra (N' * p) 2 S₀` containing $p$ and containing $T_\ell - a_\ell(W)$ for every prime $\ell \notin S_0$ with $\ell \nmid N'p$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta(W)$.
--
--   This is pure level raising at weight $2$: the mod $p$ Hecke eigensystem cut out by the Frobenius traces of $W$, realised by a maximal ideal of the weight-$2$ Hecke algebra of level $N'$, is realised again at level $N'p$, along the inclusion of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N'))$ into $S_2(\Gamma_0(N'p))$, which intertwines the $T_\ell$ for $\ell \nmid N'p$. It is the weight-$2$ branch of the weight-and-level trade used by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_mul_two_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_two_or_succ`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_mul_two_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_two_or_succ).
